.TH SERVICEWHY 1
.SH NAME
servicewhy \\- collect passive service health evidence
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B servicewhy
servicewhy --pid PID [--format json]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Collects passive process-health evidence for a service process.
.SH OPTIONS
Use \fBservicewhy --help\fR for the complete, version-specific flag list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Uses the shared CLI status convention: 0 success, 1 a completed negative finding or policy failure, 2 invalid usage, 3 a partial result, and 4 a runtime failure. Not every status applies to every command.
